1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,931
This sound was no accident.

2
00:00:01,951 --> 00:00:04,821
The idea is credited to a single man,

3
00:00:04,841 --> 00:00:08,150
and his own death was later covered up by the state.

4
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:13,827
His name was Ernst Udet.

5
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:17,367
In the First World War he shot down 62 aircraft,

6
00:00:17,387 --> 00:00:21,565
more than any other German pilot except Manfred von Richthofen.

7
00:00:21,585 --> 00:00:23,935
In America he saw dive bombers

8
00:00:23,955 --> 00:00:26,757
plunging almost vertically onto their target.

9
00:00:26,777 --> 00:00:30,407
With money from Hermann Göring, in 1933 he bought

10
00:00:30,427 --> 00:00:33,277
two of these aircraft and brought them to Germany.

11
00:00:33,297 --> 00:00:36,787
Many officers thought dive bombers were too dangerous,

12
00:00:36,807 --> 00:00:38,710
but Udet got his way.

13
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:43,542
He became the main champion of the Junkers Ju 87, the Stuka.

14
00:00:43,562 --> 00:00:46,600
Small propellers sat on its landing gear legs.

15
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,320
The airstream drove them,

16
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:52,282
and the faster the plane dived, the louder they howled.

17
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,675
They were called Jericho Trumpets.

18
00:00:54,695 --> 00:00:59,655
In Poland and France this howl spread panic among soldiers and civilians

19
00:00:59,675 --> 00:01:01,450
before a single bomb fell.

20
00:01:01,470 --> 00:01:03,510
But the sirens slowed the aircraft down,

21
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:06,872
and later they were removed from many Stukas.

22
00:01:06,892 --> 00:01:09,742
Udet rose to head of Luftwaffe equipment

23
00:01:09,762 --> 00:01:13,284
and was now responsible for all aircraft production.

24
00:01:13,304 --> 00:01:16,729
The former stunt pilot was not made for this job.

25
00:01:16,749 --> 00:01:19,519
As the Luftwaffe lost more and more aircraft,

26
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:21,172
Göring blamed him.

27
00:01:21,192 --> 00:01:25,893
On 17 November 1941, Ernst Udet shot himself.

28
00:01:25,913 --> 00:01:27,233
Officially, it was announced

29
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:31,113
that he had died in an accident while testing a new weapon.
